course: dictionary
lesson: 758
title: BCE and CE on the timeline
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: BCE stands for «Before the Common Era». It is written after a year number, so 399 BCE means 399 years before the start of our usual calendar. It means the same as BC, which stands for «before Christ».
explain: CE stands for «Common Era», and it means the same as AD. Years CE count up from the start of the calendar, while years BCE count the other way. A bigger BCE number is further back in time.
explain: «In 399 BCE a jury in Athens condemned Socrates to death.» The number 399 BCE is bigger than 50 BCE, so that trial happened longer ago than something in 50 BCE. Always check for the letters BCE, because they tell you to count backwards.
fact: BCE means Before the Common Era, and CE means Common Era.
fact: BCE means the same as BC, and CE means the same as AD.
fact: Years BCE count down towards zero: a bigger BCE number is longer ago.
fact: «The Phoenicians spread their alphabet around the Mediterranean from about 1050 BCE.»
fact: Some people prefer BCE and CE because they do not name a religion.
exercise: What does BCE stand for? | After the Common Era | Before the Coastal Era | *Before the Common Era | A type of old coin
exercise: «In 399 BCE a jury in Athens condemned Socrates to death.» Which happened longer ago, 399 BCE or 50 BCE? | They happened at the same time | Neither, because they are in the future | *399 BCE | 50 BCE
exercise: Which abbreviation means the same as AD? | BC | Before Christ | *CE | BCE
test: Which is further back in time: 1050 BCE or 1259 BCE? | They are the same time | *1259 BCE | Neither, both are in the future | 1050 BCE
test: Why do some people prefer BCE and CE? | They are only used in maths lessons | They are shorter to write than any other words | *They do not name a religion | They count forwards from zero
exam: Jayden writes «Socrates died in 399 BC». Which abbreviation means the same as BC? | *BCE | CE | AD
